<title>JAPAN: Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</title>
<headline>Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mikuni and Co Ltd said on Friday it had assigned the following preliminary ratings to planned bond issues:</p>
<p>-AA-</p>
<p>The Kansai Electric Power Co Inc, one billion Dutch guilder mortgaged due 2007.</p>
<p>-A-</p>
<p>Advantest Corp, 4.3 billion yen unsecured with warrants due 2001.  </p>
<p>-A-</p>
<p>Mitsubishi Estate Co Ltd, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2002. 20 billion yen unsecured due 2003. 30 billion yen unsecured due 2007.</p>
<p>-BBB-</p>
<p>Toc Co Ltd, 0.24 billion yen unsecured with warrants due 2000.</p>
<p>-BB-</p>
<p>Kawasaki Steel Co, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2002.  </p>
<p>-B-</p>
<p>Domy Co Ltd, 2.5 billion yen unsecured convertible due 2001, private placement.</p>
<p>Iwasaki Electric Co Ltd, 0.26 billion yen unsecured with warrants duue 2002.</p>
<p>Tokyo Tatemono Co Ltd, five billion yen unsecured due 2001.</p>
<p>Yachiyo Musen Denki Co Ltd, 0.38 billion yen unsecured with warrantts due 2000.  </p>
<p>-CCC-</p>
<p>Kawasaki Kisen Kaisha Ltd, five billion yen unsecured due 2002.</p>
</text>
